#: ../../source/fun_project/01-fun_Smart_trashcan.rst:52
msgid "3. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/01-fun_Smart_trashcan.rst:54
msgid "The project is based on real-time monitoring of the distance between an object and a trash can. An ultrasonic sensor continuously measures this distance, and if an object approaches within 20cm, the trash can interprets it as an intention to dispose of waste and automatically opens its lid. This automation adds smartness and convenience to a regular trash can."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/01-fun_Smart_trashcan.rst:56
msgid "**Initial Setup and Variable Declaration**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/01-fun_Smart_trashcan.rst:58
msgid "Here, we're including the ``Servo`` library and defining the constants and variables we'll use. The pins for the servo and the ultrasonic sensor are declared. We also have an array ``averDist`` to hold the three distance measurements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/01-fun_Smart_trashcan.rst:73
msgid "setup() Function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/01-fun_Smart_trashcan.rst:75
msgid "The ``setup()`` function initializes serial communication, configures the ultrasonic sensor's pins, and sets the initial position of the servo to the closed position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/01-fun_Smart_trashcan.rst:90
msgid "loop() Function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/01-fun_Smart_trashcan.rst:92
msgid "The ``loop()`` function is responsible for continuously measuring the distance, computing its average, and then making a decision whether to open or close the trash can's lid based on this averaged distance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/01-fun_Smart_trashcan.rst:115
msgid "Distance Reading Function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/01-fun_Smart_trashcan.rst:117
msgid "This function, ``readDistance()``, is what actually interacts with the ultrasonic sensor. It sends a pulse and waits for an echo. The time taken for the echo is then used to calculate the distance between the sensor and any object in front of it."
msgstr ""

